# TODO(exam-mode): suspended because the telecom SA labels carry different names in
# the two trees and no single static rule can satisfy both:
#   - public master : sa_telecom_tel_call_manager   (base/public/service.te:58,
#                       mapped to service 4005 in base/public/service_contexts:197)
#                     sa_telecom_tel_state_registry (telephony/telecom/public/telecom.te:14,
#                       mapped to service 4009 in base/public/service_contexts:201)
#   - inner source  : sa_foundation_tel_call_manager / sa_foundation_tel_state_registry
# The AVCs above were captured on an inner-source build, hence the sa_foundation_*
# tcontext. Using the public name fails the inner build with "unknown type" and vice
# versa. Restore both rules with the sa_foundation_* names once the rename lands in
# public master. Functional impact while suspended: assessment_service cannot get SA
# 4005/4009 from samgr, so call-state detection and the call observer are AVC-denied
# under enforcing (they still work under permissive).
# allow assessment_service sa_foundation_tel_call_manager:samgr_class { get };
# allow assessment_service sa_foundation_tel_state_registry:samgr_class { get };

