# avc:  denied  { get } for service=66818 sid=u:r:assessment_service:s0 scontext=u:r:assessment_service:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:service_66818:s0 tclass=samgr_class permissive=1
# TODO(exam-mode): dropped, not suspended for a missing type alone. service_66818 is
# a label samgr synthesises at runtime for an SAID that has no static mapping: 66818
# is absent from system_ability_definition.h and no service_contexts entry covers the
# 668xx range, so the type is undefined in this tree and referencing it fails the
# build. Writing a rule against a synthesised fallback label is also against the
# "no default label" rule. The component that owns SAID 66818 must first register a
# proper label in its own service_contexts; only then can this grant be written, and
# it should use that real label. Impact while dropped: that one SA lookup is denied
# under enforcing. Note the neighbouring sa_lowpower_manager (service 66837) is
# suspended for the same underlying reason, so both may belong to the same pending
# component.

