# avc: denied { search } for pid=13767, comm="/system/bin/sa_main"  name="/etc" dev="overlay" ino=5 scontext=u:r:assessment_service:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:vendor_etc_file:s0 tclass=dir permissive=1
# Skip: violates the multi-line neverallow in base/system/system_domain.te that ends
# with "vendor_etc_file:dir { search }". Its exclusion list covers hap_domain,
# foundation, samgr, media_service and others, but not assessment_service, and the
# compiler confirms the conflict:
#   neverallow base_typeattr_304 vendor_etc_file (dir (search))
#     allow assessment_service vendor_etc_file (dir (search))
# Note line 58 of the same file uses ~{ search getattr read open mounton relabelto },
# which does exempt search; the prohibition comes from the separate rule below it, so
# both must be read together. The sanctioned exemption is the
# vendor_etc_file_violator_dir_search attribute, which needs security review and whose
